    id: "loops",
    subject: "cpp",
    title: "Loops",
    content: "Loops repeat a block of code multiple times.\n\nThree Types of Loops:\n1. for loop: when you know the number of iterations\n2. while loop: when you don't know iterations, check before each\n3. do-while loop: execute at least once, then check\n\nfor Loop:\nfor (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\n    cout << i << \" \";\n}\nOutput: 0 1 2 3 4\n\nwhile Loop:\nint i = 0;\nwhile (i < 5) {\n    cout << i << \" \";\n    i++;\n}\nOutput: 0 1 2 3 4\n\ndo-while Loop:\nint i = 0;\ndo {\n    cout << i << \" \";\n    i++;\n} while (i < 5);\nOutput: 0 1 2 3 4\n\nInfinite Loops:\nwhile (true) { ... }     // Runs forever (use break to exit)\nfor (;;) { ... }          // Same as while(true)\n\nWhen to Use Which:\n- for: counting, iterating over ranges\n- while: unknown iterations, sentinel values\n- do-while: menu systems, input validation",
