    content: "Functions can return a value using the return statement.\n\nReturning Different Types:\nint add(int a, int b) { return a + b; }\ndouble divide(int a, int b) { return static_cast<double>(a) / b; }\nbool isPositive(int x) { return x > 0; }\nchar getGrade(int score) {\n    if (score >= 90) return 'A';\n    if (score >= 80) return 'B';\n    return 'F';\n}\n\nReturning Multiple Values:\n// Option 1: Use reference parameters\nvoid getMinMax(int a, int b, int& min, int& max) {\n    min = (a < b) ? a : b;\n    max = (a > b) ? a : b;\n}\n\n// Option 2: Use struct\nstruct Result { int min; int max; };\nResult getMinMax(int a, int b) {\n    return { min(a), b) };\n}\n\nEarly Return:\nint findIndex(int arr[], int n, int target) {\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        if (arr[i] == target) return i;  // Found it!\n    }\n    return -1;  // Not found\n}\n\nvoid process(int x) {\n    if (x < 0) return;  // Exit early if invalid\n    // ... continue processing\n}\n\nCommon Mistakes:\n- Forgetting to return a value (undefined behavior)\n- Returning reference to local variable (dangling reference)\n- Returning different types in different paths",
